310.       tempvar f13sgitmin f13sgitmax
311.       qui gegen double `f13sgitmin' = min(cond(`subgroups' >= ., ., `subgroups')) if `ifstatement' & `ttre' != ., by(`i' `t')
312.       qui gegen double `f13sgitmax' = max(cond(`subgroups' >= ., ., `subgroups')) if `ifstatement' & `ttre' != ., by(`i' `t')
313.       cap assert `f13sgitmin' == `f13sgitmax' if `ifstatement' & `ttre' != .
314.       if _rc != 0 {
315.         dis as error "Error: the subgroup variable `subgroups' varies within `i'-by-`t' cells of the treated estimation sample."
316.         dis as error "wooldid estimates effects at the `i'-by-period level, so subgroup estimates built from cells that mix subgroups cannot reflect within-cell subgroup differences - each subgroup only reweights the same pooled cell e
> ffects, and subgroup contrasts can come back identical even when true effects differ sharply by subgroup."
317.         dis as error "Define `i' at the finer level over which the subgroup varies (e.g., egen newi = group(`i' `subgroups')), or drop the subgroups() option."
318.         dis as error "To ignore this error, specify safety(off)."
319.         error 459
320.       }
321.       qui drop `f13sgitmin' `f13sgitmax'
322.     }
323.     * a unit split across multiple subgroups over time (subgroup varies within i across
.     * periods) is refused under default safety - a unit cannot belong to more than one
